bag model: a_f=1, a_t=0.3, B=1, T_c^4=4.2857; start T0^4 = 30 T_c^4 (equilibrium, false phase)
every reader uses h only, so a constant true vacuum V_t of any size never enters R (shift invariance, Lemma B);
NOTE: for IE the end value of Lam_late/rho_nc is ODE round-off: an absolute offset D is a constant, so D/rho_nc grows like e^{4u}.
      The bracket gives D relative to the initial density (the integration-constant error). Analytically D = 0 (r166_identity.out:2).
g/H^2 is computed from V' = -3h - R' and is V_t-independent.
columns: reader | min g/H^2 | max g/H^2 | Lam_late/rho_nc at u_n-4W | Lam_late/rho_nc at end | int(g/H^2)R du (= Delta V; -B means the false vacuum was absorbed) | e-folds accelerating
